Editable draw.io diagrams

Install:
  Install the missing bundled skill and global MCP package; prepare Node.js and pnpm as needed.
  Register the drawio MCP server in Codex when missing; preserve an existing drawio entry and other Codex settings.

Upgrade:
  Back up and replace the installed skill with bundled files; restore previous skill files if replacement fails.
  Update the installed MCP package and register it when its Codex entry is missing; skip absent components.

Status:
  Report skill locations based on SKILL.md presence, Node.js and MCP command locations and the Node.js version.
  Report whether drawio is registered in Codex; MCP connectivity and browser rendering are not checked.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.
  Codex CLI must already be installed; install it separately with wsley install codex.

Configuration:
  Source: https://github.com/DayuanJiang/next-ai-draw-io/tree/main/packages/mcp-server
  Destination: ~/.agents/skills/next-ai-drawio
  Existing copies at ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/skills/next-ai-drawio are consolidated into links to the destination when skill files are replaced.
  Codex configuration: ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/config.toml
  MCP server: drawio; the command uses the installed executable's absolute path.
  Back up the Codex configuration before adding the server; preserve existing tool approval settings.
  Session data and drawing preferences: ~/.next-ai-drawio/
  Preview: 127.0.0.1:6002; ports through 6020 are tried when occupied.
  A connected preview tab in a regular browser is required for live editing, screenshots and image exports.
  Remote or WSL hosts may require port forwarding or manual opening of the preview URL.
  Restart Codex after installation to load the skill and MCP tools; /mcp shows connected tools.
